{"id": 1962, "stem": "<div class=\"relative w-full min-w-0 max-w-full self-stretch\" id=\"question-text\"><span><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><mark class=\"bg-transparent dark:text-neutral-100\" data-markjs=\"true\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">A</mark> 34-year-old man comes to the emergency department due to a severe headache.\u00a0 The patient describes unbearable, throbbing pain around his right eye that awakened him.\u00a0 Over the past week, he has had several similar episodes that spontaneously resolved after 20-30 minutes.\u00a0 The patient has no other medical conditions and takes no medications.\u00a0 He smokes a pack of cigarettes daily and drinks alcohol on social occasions.\u00a0 On physical examination, the patient appears restless and paces in the room.\u00a0 There is mild conjunctival injection and miosis of the right eye.\u00a0 Neurologic examination otherwise shows no abnormalities.\u00a0 Which of the following is the most likely cause of this patient's current symptoms?\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c</p></span></div>", "options": [{"label": "A", "text": "Acute angle-closure glaucoma"}, {"label": "B", "text": "Cavernous sinus thrombosis"}, {"label": "C", "text": "Cluster headache"}, {"label": "D", "text": "Migraine without aura"}, {"label": "E", "text": "Opiate withdrawal"}, {"label": "F", "text": "Trigeminal neuralgia"}], "correctAnswer": "C", "explanation": "<div class=\"relative w-full min-w-0 max-w-full self-stretch\" id=\"question-explanation\"><span class=\"\"><div id=\"div_T46083\" style=\"overflow-x: auto; font-size: 1rem;\"><div class=\"group/triggerable\" data-is-open=\"false\"><div class=\"group/draggable\" data-is-draggable=\"true\" data-is-dragging=\"false\"><div class=\"group/resizable relative\" data-is-maximized=\"false\" data-is-resizable=\"true\" data-is-resizing=\"false\"><div class=\"relative max-w-full\"><div aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"pointer-events-none absolute left-0 top-0 bottom-0 w-8 z-10 transition-opacity duration-200 bg-gradient-to-r from-white dark:from-nbme-primary-dark-800 warm:from-egg-sour-50 to-transparent opacity-0\"></div><div aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"pointer-events-none absolute right-0 top-0 bottom-0 w-8 z-10 transition-opacity duration-200 bg-gradient-to-l from-white dark:from-nbme-primary-dark-800 warm:from-egg-sour-50 to-transparent opacity-0\"></div><div class=\"max-w-full overflow-x-auto [&amp;_td]:min-w-[8rem] [&amp;_th]:min-w-[8rem]\"><table class=\"border bg-transparent dark:text-white border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white hover:bg-transparent warm:hover:bg-transparent dark:hover:bg-transparent cursor-default mt-2 mb-3\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><tbody style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><tr class=\"hover:bg-original-nbme-400/10 warm:hover:bg-brown-700/10 dark:hover:bg-white/15\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" colspan=\"4\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><mark class=\"bg-transparent dark:text-neutral-50\" data-markjs=\"true\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">T</mark>ypes of headache</strong></p></td></tr><tr class=\"hover:bg-original-nbme-400/10 warm:hover:bg-brown-700/10 dark:hover:bg-white/15\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"></td><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Migraine</strong></p></td><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Cluster</strong></p></td><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Tension</strong></p></td></tr><tr class=\"hover:bg-original-nbme-400/10 warm:hover:bg-brown-700/10 dark:hover:bg-white/15\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Sex predilection</strong></p></td><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\">Female &gt; male</p></td><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\">Male &gt; female</p></td><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\">Female &gt; male</p></td></tr><tr class=\"hover:bg-original-nbme-400/10 warm:hover:bg-brown-700/10 dark:hover:bg-white/15\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Family history</strong></p></td><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\">Often present</p></td><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\">\u00b1</p></td><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\">None</p></td></tr><tr class=\"hover:bg-original-nbme-400/10 warm:hover:bg-brown-700/10 dark:hover:bg-white/15\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Onset</strong></p></td><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\">Variable</p></td><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\">During sleep or similar timing daily</p></td><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\">Under stress</p></td></tr><tr class=\"hover:bg-original-nbme-400/10 warm:hover:bg-brown-700/10 dark:hover:bg-white/15\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Location</strong></p></td><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\">Often unilateral</p></td><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\">Behind one eye</p></td><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\">Band-like pattern around the head (bilateral)</p></td></tr><tr class=\"hover:bg-original-nbme-400/10 warm:hover:bg-brown-700/10 dark:hover:bg-white/15\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Character</strong></p></td><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\">Pulsatile &amp; throbbing</p></td><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\">Excruciating, sharp &amp; steady</p></td><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\">Dull, tight &amp; persistent</p></td></tr><tr class=\"hover:bg-original-nbme-400/10 warm:hover:bg-brown-700/10 dark:hover:bg-white/15\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Duration</strong></p></td><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\">4-72 hr</p></td><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\">15-180 min</p></td><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\">30 min to months/years</p></td></tr><tr class=\"hover:bg-original-nbme-400/10 warm:hover:bg-brown-700/10 dark:hover:bg-white/15\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Associatedsymptoms</strong></p></td><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\">Photophobia, phonophobia &amp; nausea, \u00b1 aura</p></td><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\">Ipsilateral sweating, facial flushing, nasal congestion, pupillary changes &amp; lacrimation</p></td><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\">Muscle tenderness in the head, neck, or shoulders</p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div></div></div></div></div><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\">This patient has recurrent, unilateral, periorbital headaches associated with autonomic symptoms (eg, miosis, conjunctival injection) and restlessness, a classic presentation of <strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">cluster headaches</strong>.</p><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\">Cluster headaches occur in greater frequency in men than in women.\u00a0 Patients usually describe <strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">severe periorbital</strong> pain (ie, V1 division of the <a class=\"hint\" data-exhibit-id=\"exhibit-ljurcy5yjvlopo6ubtekhun7\" href=\"#exhibit-exhibit-ljurcy5yjvlopo6ubtekhun7\">trigeminal nerve</a>) with a sharp or stabbing quality, typically lasting 15-90 minutes.\u00a0 Onset during sleep is common.\u00a0 The headaches often occur <strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">multiple times</strong> per day for several weeks (ie, in clusters) and are followed by a long period of remission.</p><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Ipsilateral autonomic symptoms</strong> are almost always present, probably because trigeminal nociceptors activate <strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">parasympathetic</strong> pathways in the brainstem.\u00a0 This often manifests similar to <a class=\"hint\" data-exhibit-id=\"exhibit-cz9et3p5eqjbdh9q5pmppaoz\" href=\"#exhibit-exhibit-cz9et3p5eqjbdh9q5pmppaoz\">Horner syndrome</a> (ptosis, miosis).\u00a0 Nasal congestion, lacrimation, and conjunctival injection also commonly occur.\u00a0 The <strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">hypothalamus</strong> and suprachiasmatic nucleus also seem to be involved, which may contribute to both the <strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">restlessness/agitation</strong> and the seasonal (same time of year) or circadian (same time of day) regularity of the episodes.</p><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">(Choice A)</strong>\u00a0 Although eye pain and redness are common in acute angle-closure glaucoma, patients usually have decreased visual acuity with halos and a fixed, middilated (not constricted) pupil.</p><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">(Choice B)</strong>\u00a0 Cavernous sinus thrombosis typically occurs in patients with thrombophilia (eg, malignancy, antithrombin deficiency) or as a septic thrombosis related to a sinus infection or facial cellulitis.\u00a0 Headache is common; however, multiple cranial nerves that travel through the <a class=\"hint\" data-exhibit-id=\"exhibit-wqcioy9tjix9c0bhnnc9stl7\" href=\"#exhibit-exhibit-wqcioy9tjix9c0bhnnc9stl7\">cavernous sinus</a> are typically involved, leading to decreased facial sensation and restricted eye movements.\u00a0 Periorbital swelling, fever, and proptosis are other frequent findings.</p><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">(Choice D)</strong>\u00a0 Migraine without aura typically causes severe pulsatile, unilateral headaches often associated with photophobia, phonophobia, nausea, and vomiting.\u00a0 Although this patient describes throbbing pain, he has autonomic features (miosis, lacrimation) classic for cluster headaches rather than migraines.</p><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">(Choice E)</strong>\u00a0 Opiate withdrawal can cause lacrimation, rhinorrhea, and diaphoresis but would usually cause bilateral symptoms.\u00a0 It typically also causes gastrointestinal symptoms (eg, diarrhea, nausea), piloerection, and mydriasis; orbital pain is unexpected.</p><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">(Choice F)</strong>\u00a0 <a class=\"hint\" data-exhibit-id=\"exhibit-luub2gtszwany2st29se0vze\" href=\"#exhibit-exhibit-luub2gtszwany2st29se0vze\">Trigeminal neuralgia</a> causes sudden \"electric\" pain in the distribution of the maxillary and/or mandibular divisions of the trigeminal nerve, often preceded by light touch.\u00a0 Episodes last for seconds and do not typically occur during sleep.</p><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Educational objective:</strong>Cluster headaches cause severe unilateral periorbital pain associated with ipsilateral autonomic symptoms (eg, lacrimation, nasal congestion, miosis, conjunctival injection).\u00a0 The headaches typically last 15-180 minutes and tend to occur in clusters (multiple times per day for a few weeks).\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c</p></span></div>", "educationalObjective": "Cluster headaches cause severe unilateral periorbital pain associated with ipsilateral autonomic symptoms (eg, lacrimation, nasal congestion, miosis, conjunctival injection).  The headaches typically last 15-180 minutes and tend to occur in clusters (multiple times per day for a few weeks).\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c", "subject": "Pathology", "system": "Nervous System", "topic": "Cluster headache", "category": "Headache", "peerCorrect": 80.0}